    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295">

                <pb facs="0537" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Soong</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Presidents Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-20">June 20, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hopkins</hi>: I am sending you a memorandum
                    which will you please present at your discretion to the President and the Prime
                    Minister, as I think it is important for me to participate with them in
                    discussions affecting China.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d295-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>With kind regards,</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tse Vun Soong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d295-a1.xml" xpointer="d295-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d295-f1" n="1" xml:id="d295-f1-content">
                <p>Soong, who was in the United States on a special mission in connection with
                    securing wartime assistance for the Chinese Government, met with Roosevelt,
                    Churchill, and Hopkins on the morning of June 22, 1942; see the editorial note,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg438">p. 438</ref>. Soong
                    also attended the meeting of the Pacific War Council on June 25, for the record
                    of which see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg448">p.
                        448</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
